# Part VII ch. 7, step C8: a `via` trait that does not give the method. `^Named` asks
# `Name` and `Greeting`; the via definitions from `^Titled` give `Name` alone, so `derive
# ^Named via ^Titled for Book` leaves `Greeting` without a definition, and the checker
# refuses the derive line. The form of the via definitions is Claude's first ruling, as in
# conformance/doc-c8-derive-via.
# The expected diagnostic is hand-derived: its text is Claude's, the error a derive gets.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
trait ^Named a:
    Name: fn a -> Text
    Greeting: fn a -> Text

trait ^Titled a:
    Title: fn a -> Text

derive ^Named a via ^Titled a:
    fn Name x = Title x

type Book = record:
    title: Text

impl ^Titled Book:
    fn Title book = book.title

derive ^Named via ^Titled for Book
